{"name":"Hazelnut Milk","hex":"#eeaa77","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"hazelnut milk","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A milky liquid made from hazelnuts and used as a milk substitute, cooking ingredient or beverage."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hazelnut_milk"}],"entries":[{"title":"Plant milk","blocks":[{"text":"Plant milk is a category of non-dairy beverages made from a water-based plant extract for flavoring and aroma. Nut milk is a subcategory made from nuts, while other plant milks may be created from grains, pseudocereals, legumes, seeds or endosperm. Plant-based milks are consumed as alternatives to dairy milk and provide similar qualities, such as a creamy mouthfeel, as well as a bland or palatable taste. Many are sweetened or flavored."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/Cononut_milk.JPG/330px-Cononut_milk.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Plant_milk","wikidata":"Q2640574"},{"title":"Hazelnut","blocks":[{"text":"The hazelnut is the fruit of the hazel tree and therefore includes any of the nuts deriving from species of the genus Corylus, especially the nuts of the species Corylus avellana. They are also known as cobnuts or filberts according to species."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e4/Hazelnuts_%28Corylus_avellana%29_-_whole_with_kernels.jpg/330px-Hazelnuts_%28Corylus_avellana%29_-_whole_with_kernels.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hazelnut","wikidata":"Q578307"},{"title":"Milk","blocks":[{"text":"Milk is usually a white liquid food produced by the mammary glands of lactating mammals. It is the primary source of nutrition for young mammals before they are able to digest solid food. Milk contains many nutrients, including calcium and protein, as well as lactose and saturated fat; the enzyme lactase is needed to break down lactose. Immune factors and immune-modulating components in milk contribute to milk immunity. The first milk, which is called colostrum, contains antibodies and immune-modulating components that strengthen the immune system against many diseases."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a5/Glass_of_Milk_%2833657535532%29.jpg/330px-Glass_of_Milk_%2833657535532%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Milk","wikidata":"Q8495"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/Amazake_by_emily_harbour_in_july.jpg/500px-Amazake_by_emily_harbour_in_july.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/Amazake_by_emily_harbour_in_july.jpg/1280px-Amazake_by_emily_harbour_in_july.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/Amazake_by_emily_harbour_in_july.jpg/500px-Amazake_by_emily_harbour_in_july.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Amazake, Japanese rice milk","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAmazake_by_emily_harbour_in_july.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/13/Barley_milk.jpg/500px-Barley_milk.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/13/Barley_milk.jpg/1280px-Barley_milk.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/13/Barley_milk.jpg/500px-Barley_milk.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Barley milk","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABarley_milk.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipe